<%# card--wide for the same reason as "my games": this card holds the widest
    thing on the dashboard once each game is a panel of its own, and half a
    grid gave the game names and their teams a column too narrow to sit side
    by side. See .dash-grid in screens.css. %>
<fieldset class="card card--wide">
  <legend>
    <%= t("games.teams.legend") %>
  </legend>

  <%# One panel per game, rather than a heading and a list repeated down a
      single column. .team-group carried no styling at all before, so a game's
      name and the team names under it stacked with nothing between them --
      the reported problem was not being able to tell which teams belonged to
      which game, and with two games the reading order alone said nothing.

      Nested surface, following .team-panel on the operator screen: a --panel
      on --surface-2 inside a --card on --surface. Both contrast pairs are
      already accounted for in tokens.css.

      The <h3> stays a direct child of this div: the grouping spec in
      spec/requests/dashboard_teams_by_game_spec.rb finds a game's heading by
      text and walks to its nearest li/div/section ancestor to assert that a
      team is under the right game. That ancestor must remain the element that
      wraps this game and only this game. %>
  <div class="team-groups">
    <% teams_by_game.each do |game, teams| %>
      <div class="panel team-group">
        <h3><%= game.name %></h3>
        <%# Team names are plain, and the <strong> they used to carry is gone
            on purpose. h3 is weight 600 and a browser's default <strong> is
            700, so every team name was rendering BOLDER than the game it
            belonged to -- the heading lost to its own list, which is most of
            why the grouping did not read. The panel's heading is now the only
            bold thing in it.

            Nothing asserts on the tag: the grouping spec matches with
            have_text. %>
        <ul class="game-list">
          <% teams.each do |team| %>
            <li>
              <%= team.name %>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</fieldset>
